      "writtenOn": "2020-04-06T14:49:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see. In this change, apexDepsMutator() is changed as well to check:\n\n  (cur.DepIsInSameApex(mctx, child) || inAnySdk(child))\n\nSo, it is when DepIsInSameApex \u003d\u003d false and inAnySdk \u003d\u003d true.\n\nThe reason why walkPayloadDeps uses `ApexName() !\u003d \"\"` was the bug of WalkDeps, which you\u0027ve already fixed. We could revert the line: https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/build/soong/+/1252774/5/apex/apex.go#b1967\n\nI\u0027m curious if there are other cases like SDK members which have apex variants but not supposed to be part of the apex. If SDK is the only case, can we avoid making apex variants of SDK members? It seems necessary for SDK\u0027s ReplaceDependencies to work though.",
      "parentUuid": "80de8027_e276b1e0",
